      "content": "MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Motion is systematically analyzed across 1D and 2D frameworks, including uniform circular motion.",
        "A fundamental distinction is drawn between scalar quantities (distance, speed) and vector quantities (displacement, velocity).",
        "Equations of motion apply specifically to scenarios with uniform acceleration and motion under gravity.",
        "Graphical representations and unit conversions serve as indispensable analytical tools for competitive exam questions."
      ],
      "id": "1clm4ye"
    },
