    },
    {
      "id": "kvbzxx9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "1. TYPES OF MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pjl2ljv",
      "content": "• Linear Motion – Motion in a straight line."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uo8j3a9",
      "content": "• Circular Motion – Motion along circular path."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "burmv5c",
      "content": "• Rotational Motion – Motion about an axis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f2ifl1j",
      "content": "• Periodic Motion – Motion that repeats at regular intervals."
    },
    {
      "id": "487p4dc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2. DISTANCE AND DISPLACEMENT"
    },
    {
      "id": "6yqpyy5",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Feature</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Distance</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Displacement</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Definition</p>",
            "<p>Total path travelled</p>",
            "<p>Shortest path between two points</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Nature</p>",
            "<p>Scalar Quantity</p>",
            "<p>Vector Quantity</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "y2y98r8",
      "content": "SI Unit: metre (m)"
    },
    {
      "id": "jjwyznz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "3. SPEED AND VELOCITY"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "dz3e7h6",
      "content": "Speed = Distance / Time"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "iw02v4l",
      "content": "Velocity = Displacement / Time"
    },
    {
      "id": "ph1h4l5",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Feature</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Speed</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Velocity</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Nature</p>",
            "<p>Scalar</p>",
            "<p>Vector</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Depends on</p>",
            "<p>Distance</p>",
            "<p>Displacement</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "pf2kahx",
      "content": "SI Unit: m/s"
    },
    {
      "id": "2opdkk8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4. ACCELERATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rduqbv0",
      "content": "Acceleration = (Final Velocity – Initial Velocity) / Time"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5y8852e",
      "content": "a = (v – u) / t"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "rwtt0sf",
      "content": "SI Unit: m/s²"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "919w74u",
      "content": "Positive acceleration → Speed increases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f7w594j",
      "content": "Negative acceleration (Retardation) → Speed decreases"
    },
    {
      "id": "4kklkip",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5. EQUATIONS OF MOTION (Uniform Acceleration)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2sacv8v",
      "content": "v = u + at"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pxv05ro",
      "content": "s = ut + ½ at²"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8bdix2y",
      "content": "v² = u² + 2as"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9g1k01k",
      "content": "Where:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "gl978ia",
      "content": "u = Initial velocity"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "lhn5e3z",
      "content": "v = Final velocity"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "7peu9u0",
      "content": "a = Acceleration"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "s9rddb4",
      "content": "t = Time"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "0kpno8b",
      "content": "s = Displacement"
    },
    {
      "id": "pe3k24n",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "6. MOTION UNDER GRAVITY (FREE FALL)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nht5yo8",
      "content": "When a body falls freely under gravity, acceleration = g = 9.8 m/s²"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "lg12t2g",
      "content": "v = gt"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4txx2ug",
      "content": "s = ½ gt²"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "dhzjk73",
      "content": "v² = 2gh"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dmgn58m",
      "content": "All bodies fall with same acceleration in vacuum."
    },
    {
      "id": "udwirq2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "7. UNIFORM CIRCULAR MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dr1ylry",
      "content": "In uniform circular motion, speed remains constant but direction changes. Hence velocity changes and acceleration exists (centripetal acceleration)."
    },
    {
      "id": "hefvhpt",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "8. GRAPHICAL REPRESENTATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mldvrc8",
      "content": "Distance-Time Graph:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tpj8z4k",
      "content": "• Straight line → Uniform motion"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "10o0w03",
      "content": "• Curve → Non-uniform motion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9qn21yr",
      "content": "Velocity-Time Graph: "
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mtwikoe",
      "content": "• Straight line → Uniform acceleration"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ej5dswd",
      "content": "• Area under graph = Displacement"
    },
    {
      "id": "qafmj29",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "9.SCALAR AND VECTOR QUANTITIES"
    },
    {
      "id": "nebkqpo",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Feature</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Scalar</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Vector</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Definition</p>",
            "<p>Magnitude only</p>",
            "<p>Magnitude + Direction</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Examples</p>",
            "<p>Distance, Speed, Time</p>",
            "<p>Displacement, Velocity, Acceleration</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "9o1k0hk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "10. AVERAGE SPEED & INSTANTANEOUS VELOCITY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vjem21z",
      "content": "Average Speed = Total Distance / Total Time"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j7uixf7",
      "content": "Average Velocity = Total Displacement / Total Time"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g5yrp2g",
      "content": "Instantaneous Velocity = Velocity at a particular instant of time"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "edag9d7",
      "content": "Important RRB Concept:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3226a28",
      "content": "• If a body travels equal distances at speeds v1 and v2,"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Concept Pair",
        "Scalar Quantity",
        "Vector Quantity"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Position / Path",
          "Distance",
          "Displacement"
        ],
        [
          "Rate of Motion",
          "Speed",
          "Velocity"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "b1o18on"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6x9c79c",
      "content": "  Average Speed = 2v1v2 / (v1 + v2)"
    },
    {
      "id": "s0ebkxs",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "11. RELATIVE MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7njbws0",
      "content": "Relative motion is the motion of an object with respect to another object."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cr52o93",
      "content": "Relative Velocity (same direction) = v1 – v2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bgihmps",
      "content": "Relative Velocity (opposite direction) = v1 + v2"
    },
    {
      "id": "amb9vz7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "12. MOTION IN 1D AND 2D"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5p4yhtm",
      "content": "1D Motion – Motion along straight line."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ykh47b1",
      "content": "2D Motion – Motion in a plane (Projectile motion conceptually)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5766zmr",
      "content": "Projectile Important Points:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r2tsqwb",
      "content": "• Horizontal velocity remains constant."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "odi6xjd",
      "content": "• Vertical motion affected by gravity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kz5omor",
      "content": "• Time of flight = 2u sinθ / g"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "727lsnf",
      "content": "• Maximum height = u² sin²θ / 2g<img></img>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zyzoleu",
      "content": "• Range = u² sin2θ / g"
    },
    {
      "id": "3brlu4y",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "13. UNIFORM CIRCULAR MOTION – FORMULAS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3eb7dg4",
      "content": "Centripetal Acceleration (a) = v² / r"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "al5plqz",
      "content": "Centripetal Force (F) = mv² / r"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tz6ark8",
      "content": "Direction always towards centre."
    },
    {
      "id": "g5jng3e",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "14. GRAPH CONCEPTS (VERY IMPORTANT FOR RRB)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rg18be3",
      "content": "• Slope of Distance-Time Graph = Speed"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bc3rwxa",
      "content": "• Slope of Velocity-Time Graph = Acceleration"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jqhjyqf",
      "content": "• Area under Velocity-Time Graph = Displacement"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yypm4f5",
      "content": "• Horizontal line in v-t graph = Constant velocity"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Graphical interpretation (Position-Time & Velocity-Time) is extremely high-yield for RRB exams.",
        "Questions frequently contrast scalar vs. vector properties (e.g., Distance vs. Displacement, Speed vs. Velocity).",
        "Special tricky points often focus on unit conversion errors and sign conventions in free-fall motion under gravity."
      ],
      "id": "o2kzlaf"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y5zi7kv",
      "content": "• Negative slope in v-t graph = Retardation"
    },
    {
      "id": "0k7ac61",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "15. IMPORTANT UNIT CONVERSIONS"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "gby6iyb",
      "content": "1 km/h = 5/18 m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "yf6fg0n",
      "content": "1 m/s = 18/5 km/h"
    },
    {
      "id": "zspv96u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "16. SPECIAL RRB TRICKY POINTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9er4mep",
      "content": "• At highest point of projectile, vertical velocity = 0."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wvicu4o",
      "content": "• In uniform motion, acceleration = 0."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "751mumo",
      "content": "• A body can have zero velocity but non-zero acceleration."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lno8pz3",
      "content": "• Speed is never negative, velocity can be negative."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s4x9amj",
      "content": "• If displacement is zero, average velocity is zero but distance may not be zero."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kzkulv0",
      "content": "• State of rest is zero velocity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lr9mvph",
      "content": "• At highest point of vertical throw, velocity = 0 but acceleration = g."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zzpjk9l",
      "content": "• In circular motion, acceleration acts towards centre."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aa4ro1f",
      "content": "• Scalar quantities: Distance, Speed."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7h8016f",
      "content": "• Vector quantities: Displacement, Velocity, Acceleration."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}